+**⟶ AND THIS SAME SECTION CARRIES `P-2`'S TWO REPAIRS — 2026-11-17, `D-198`, THE ARCHITECT, VERBATIM: *"Take default and continue"*, AND `D-198` ITEM 4 PRINTS THE CLASS SEPARATELY FROM THIS SECTION'S.** **`P-2` IS NOT A THIRD BEHAVIOUR CHANGE BESIDE `P-3`'S; IT IS TWO DEFECTS REPAIRED IN WHAT `1.11.0` ALREADY SHIPPED** (`D-197` item 1: the creation's build → sweep → save → deliver order is the shipped one), **so a reader who takes this section as ONE landing is reading it right — the two repairs ride the same cut and each is a sentence a consumer can act on.**
+
+5. **A REFUSED CONSTRUCTION NOW REMOVES THE FILE IT CREATED — ON EVERY ARM — AND NEVER TOUCHES A FILE THAT WAS THERE BEFORE YOUR CALL.** `D-198` item 1's rule is one: *"the file a construction CREATED is removed on EVERY refusal the construction reaches after the create, and ONLY that file"*, and its ground is `A55` read at *"what the construction CAUSES"* — the file's existence is caused by the call, the refusal is the call's answer, and no caller data is in it. **BEFORE THIS RELEASE THE TREE HELD THREE DISPOSITIONS FOR ONE STATE**: a construction refused **after a round had already run** (rank `20` `ConstraintPassRefused`, the cycle and the post-round inconsistency) **left the created file standing**; **every other refusing arm removed it**; and a **creation-fired listener body that threw** (rank `21` `ListenerBodyThrew`) **left it standing**. **THE LINE BETWEEN THE FIRST TWO WAS A STATUS COMPARISON INSIDE A REFUSAL CONVERSION — which is nobody's decision — so the rule is now stated once, at the frame that owns the file's whole lifetime.** **THE MIGRATION SENTENCE, SO YOU CAN TELL WHICH BEHAVIOUR YOUR VERSION HAS:** *"If you construct with a `filePath`, carry constraints, and the construction refuses, the file used to be left behind on some refusing arms and not others; it is now always removed — the file is the construction's own, and a file that was there before your call is never touched."* **WHAT DOES NOT MOVE: a passing registration's already-saved `file` landing stands** — no rollback composes at the delivery seat and a removal is not a save's undo — **and a file your own call did not create is never removed, on any arm**, which is the guard's `existed` bound and the half that protects your data (`CAW-3`).
