+
+**AND `P-2`'S CLASS IS PRINTED SEPARATELY, BECAUSE `D-126` ITEM 3'S ARITHMETIC MAKES A VERSION THE MAXIMUM OF THE MOVES IT CARRIES AND THIS SECTION'S OWN MOVE IS THE LARGER.** **`P-2`'S CONTENT IS `MINOR` AND IT ADDS, REMOVES AND RENAMES NO PUBLISHED MEMBER** — one side effect of a refusal and one resolution test — **and by that arithmetic it rides `3.0.0` beside `D-193`/`D-195`'s `MAJOR`, with the two classes printed separately and neither one folded into the other** (`docs/L3/creation-as-write/design.md` §7; `D-198` item 4). **THE NUMBER IS THE ARCHITECT'S AND NO PASS MINTS IT**: `2.0.0` is spent and `3.0.0` is the larger move's line.
+
+**THE CELLS THAT CARRY THIS SECTION'S TWO REPAIRS, NAMED SO THE TURN IS AUDITABLE.** `CAW-1`…`CAW-8` (`tests/e2e/creation-as-write.test.mjs`, with `CAW-7`'s one instrument in `tests/e2e/creation-as-write-support.mjs`): `CAW-1` the rank-`20` arm leaves no file · `CAW-2` the rank-`21` arm leaves no file · `CAW-3` a pre-existing file's bytes unmoved at both · `CAW-4` a boot carrying no constraints still fires once · `CAW-5` the scalar above the watched address is silent · `CAW-6` a `mem` repair leaves the created file at `0` bytes · `CAW-7` a creation's attempts are unnameable · `CAW-8` the repair's empty set beside the creation's one delivery. **AND FOUR EXISTING CELLS ARE RE-DERIVED RATHER THAN WEAKENED**: `CSW-20`, `CSW-19` and `CSW-10` lose the standing-bytes limb — that limb was `PIN-12`'s first clause, re-spelt by `D-198` item 1 — and gain the pre-existing-file limb, and `FSC-ARM1-D`/`FSC-ARM1-ONCE` are re-derived the same way because their evidence for the carry's save was that same limb (`docs/L3/creation-as-write/design.md` §6's census names three and the measurement found five).
+
 **AND WHAT DOES NOT MOVE, NAMED SO THE NARROWING IS NOT READ WIDER THAN IT IS.**
 - **THE TOUCHED ARM IS NOT NARROWED.** A registration at a node a second identical STRUCTURED write creates or purges below it is still told, because those nodes *"exist after the write and did not before"* (`D-66`). **A re-write of the same object at `['a']` still fires a listener bound at `['a','b','c']`.**
 - **THE `delete` IS UNMOVED.** Its receipt is computed on the same one predicate and answers the act's value position `true` — a delete that removes at least one version moved the value at its address — **and a delete that removed nothing still carries `triggered: []`** (`D-3`).
